# WLISTTY.KEY - a row of a list window dragged once the window has
# scrolled within the rows it holds (TEST/WLISTT.C /DRAG, eleven items,
# WLLONG.REQ after the seed): TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/WLISTTY.SNP, checked by
# TEST/dragchk.py.  Two DOWNs leave rows 2 and 3 in the box, the pager's
# first row 1; dragged over the box's second row the drag reads row 3's
# key, the pager's row first + 1 and not the box's; ESC ends it with the
# selection still on row 2, the one pressed, which ENTER opens.
S START
K DOWN DOWN
S SCROLLED
M 1.1 DOWN ROW 0
M 1.1 MOVE ROW 0 8 0
M 1.1 MOVE ROW 1
S OVER1
K ESC
S ESC
M 1.1 UP ROW 1
K ENTER
S OPEN
K ESC
